st unscored prompt, hand the model what it produced, file the revision as the next version — so triggering it repeatedly accumulates `DIR/v0, v1, …` each with its prompt, its output and a scorecard for BOTH sets, plus `DIR/index.json` putting every version side by side. That side-by-side is the point: overfitting is the shape where `tune` improves and `holdout` does not, and walking back needs the losing versions still on disk. The reviser is told that extracting NOTHING scores perfectly on every number and is the worst outcome, and is shown the names that survived, because a model optimising counts alone will otherwise tighten until nothing does. `--as-user` reads with that person's access scopes applied (omitted ⇒ unscoped, the operator's own view). **The config is resolved `--config` > `$WORKSPACE_APP_CONFIG` > `./config.yaml` in the CURRENT directory** — so running it from a worktree (which has no `config.yaml`) would otherwise read an empty in-memory store and report a corpus with no documents; it prints which file it read and refuses up front when none configures a store.
